  "label": "User projected onto the textual message promoting religious scapegoating",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material that explicitly promotes a hateful narrative of blaming Hindus and absolving minorities in religion-based riots. The text directly addresses the user by implying they are part of or should accept this divisive ideology, even though no explicit deictic pronoun like 'you' or 'me' is present. The projection is inferred from the confrontational and accusatory tone of the text, which positions the viewer as a participant in or complicit with the 'divide and rule' strategy.",
